# Replace room.yourdomain.com with your real subdomain, pointed at this
# instance's Elastic IP via a DNS A record (see DEPLOY.md's AWS walkthrough).
#
# That's the whole config Caddy needs. Unlike nginx, Caddy's reverse_proxy
# detects and transparently forwards WebSocket upgrade requests (the
# Connection: Upgrade / Upgrade: websocket headers) with no special
# directive — and it provisions and auto-renews a real Let's Encrypt
# certificate for the domain the moment it starts, from this one block.
room.yourdomain.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:1999
}
